From 181dda224c84c30d24ad417f7c1478639258afe3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Catrysse <jan.catrysse@geoxyz.eu>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 12:12:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Show the Git branches that contain a revision (#5386).

The revision page shows a commit's id, its parents and its children; an
issue's associated revisions show the revision and a link to its diff.
Neither says which branches the commit is reachable from, so "has this fix
landed on the release branch?" cannot be answered without leaving Redmine.

GitAdapter#branches_containing runs "git branch --no-color --contains" and
returns the branch names as UTF-8. Changeset#branches asks the adapter when
it responds to that, so the other five adapters are unaffected and a
Mercurial implementation would need nothing else. Two settings decide where
the list is rendered, both off by default: display_revision_branches on the
revision page, display_associated_revision_branches in the associated
revisions of an issue. They are separate because their cost differs in kind
-- the second runs one command per revision shown.

Nothing is cached. Note-17 on this issue rejects storing branch membership
because a deleted or force-pushed branch then leaves Redmine showing a
branch the repository no longer has, with no event to correct it. Note-18
warns about the cost of running the command repeatedly, and note-20 observes
that repository pages already run several Git commands; hence the command on
demand, off by default, and split over two settings.

revision_branches_excluded drops branch names an administrator is not
interested in, as a comma separated list of names or patterns, with
revision_branches_enable_regex switching between shell style wildcards and
regular expressions. This is the pair mail_handler_excluded_filenames and
mail_handler_enable_regex_excluded_filenames already form, down to the
anchoring and the case insensitive match. An invalid regular expression is
logged and skipped rather than raised, since this one runs while a page is
being rendered.
